# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-user preference notes. Deliberately NOT shipped: this file records one person's
# taste (see tools/prose/PREFERENCES.md for the contract), and a clone of this repo must
# get Incunabula exactly as tested. Its absence is indistinguishable from a user with no
# preferences, which is the correct default -- shipping it would make taste a default.
USER_PREFERENCES.md

# The author's own record, kept beside the framework rather than shipped inside it.
# Everything in .private/ is yours: your ERRATA ledger, your commonplace book, your
# known findings, your freeze history, your registry and your books. The repository
# carries templates at the canonical paths so the tools keep working, and the real
# content lives here, untracked. See .private/README.md for what is in it.
.private/

# Your books. The framework does not ship them: a clone gets the checks, the skills and
# a scaffold command, and nothing that belongs to anyone else.
test-books/
demo-books/

# Book-carried copies of the calibration corpus. Same class as the corpus/ rule in
# tools/prose/calibration/.gitignore: published commercial prose that is nobody else's
# to ship, wherever it gets copied to. The copies stay on disk (the local controls that
# read them keep working); they are excluded from every commit. Found by reading the
# commit output for 96f549b, which carried 102 elaina files inside test-books/.
test-books/**/tools/calibration/corpus/

# Private registry exemptions: books on disk this public repo must not name.
# Read by tools/check-registry.py (load_private_dirs); see BOOKS.yaml header.
.registry-private
